Z||000006||2birds||06-20-2000||01:02 AM||||I just replaced my front engine mount, and the first one (Sealed Power) didn't line up with the existing holes on either the engine front bracket or the cradle.  I made the drive and checked the brand Autozone carries, and it is a perfect match.  Checked on the steering rack, and it's really $114, pick your desired ratio.  Only problem is the supplier is out (maybe 2 weeks).  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||06-20-2000||01:06 AM||||I agree. How many autoparts places do you think carry a rebuild kit for the rear brake calipers on an 88 Fiero V6? One of the 24 hour Autozones here in Memphis did! Not only that, but it was $6 each!<BR>Autozone has gotten MUCH MUCH MUCH better within the last couple of years...they ALWAYS have the parts I need! thumbs up!||||reg||1
Z||000008||dogtired||06-20-2000||01:26 AM||||I always price several stores and usually end up back at AutoZone  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Depends on what I am shoping for!<P>I still have several extra Booklets and Keys<BR>Let me know if you can't get one.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000009||BN Boomer||06-20-2000||03:29 AM||||We don't have AutoZone's up here in the Pacific Northwest, or at least not in the Puget Sound region. I've shopped at their stores in other parts of the country and have been quite satisfied with their service.<P>I was disappointed that the Checker/Schucks/Kragen chain bought out the local chain of Al's Auto Supply stores instead of getting someone like AutoZone in here. It seemed like everywhere there was a Schucks there was also an Al's, so all this seems to have accomplished is to reduce both Schuck's competition and our choices of stores. Oh well, maybe someday AutoZone will give 'em some real competition.<P>I don't know why someone was badmouthing NAPA above, either. In my opinion, they carry quality parts at good prices, too. I've always liked them.<P>I'd take you up on the offer for the free code reader, but somehow I suspect it would be rather useless and pale compared to the AutoXray EZ-Link Pro-Pak I bought last month. Now <B>that</B> is a code reader!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||8
Z||000010||Gokart||06-20-2000||06:06 AM||||Haze, what I meant about NAPA and painting is that they MIX paint. Had to have them mix me a quart for my trunk scoop. What a headache. Autozone only has Dupli-color and Krylon spray cans. Med red(9077) is no longer made in touch up cans. If Autozone started mixing paint, they'd probably put NAPA out of business <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 06-20-2000).]||||reg||1
